  photo: ["You move the lamp closer to pondweed in sodium hydrogencarbonate solution. What happens first?", ["More bubbles per minute, until another factor limits the rate", "Fewer bubbles, because strong light stops chlorophyll", "No change, because plants do not use light intensity", "Only respiration changes, not photosynthesis"], "Higher light intensity increases photosynthesis until CO₂ or temperature becomes limiting.", "drag the lamp-distance slider."],
